# AlpacaBridge C++ style (C++20).
#
# Captures the conventions already in the tree so adoption is a no-op for
# existing code: 4-space indent, attached (K&R) braces, pointer binds to the
# type (`char* p`), ~120 column target. Enforced incrementally in CI via
# git-clang-format, which only reformats lines touched by a PR — so turning
# this on does not churn the existing codebase.
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Google
Standard: c++20
IndentWidth: 4
TabWidth: 4
UseTab: Never
ColumnLimit: 120
AccessModifierOffset: -4
PointerAlignment: Left
DerivePointerAlignment: false
